    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0188" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/831</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 128</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-10-02">October 2,
                        1936</date>.<lb/>[Received October 9.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that Admiral
                        Bellairs,<anchor n="11" xml:id="d103-f1"/> who accompanied the British
                    Delegation to the Assembly, called on me today to give me an account of the
                    British conversations with the <pb facs="0189" n="109" xml:id="pg109"/>
                    Continental Naval Powers in respect to aligning those Powers with the British
                    naval strength, with the ultimate expectation of gaining general agreement to
                    the London 1936 Naval Treaty.</p>
                <p>I append hereto a memorandum of the conversation prepared by Mr. Reber.<anchor
                        n="12" xml:id="d103-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh</hi> R. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d103-a1.xml" xpointer="d103-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d103-f1" n="11" xml:id="d103-f1-content">
                <p>Rear Adm. R. M. Bellairs, British naval representative on the Permanent Advisory
                    Committee of the League of Nations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d103-f2" n="12" xml:id="d103-f2-content">
                <p>Samuel Reber, Second Secretary of the American Embassy in Italy, temporarily at
                    Geneva; Mr. Reber had been technical assistant for the Department of State at
                    the Naval Conference.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
